    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/949/cw/en/job/589556/senior-specialist-procurement-sourcing": {
      "title": "Senior Specialist, Procurement & Sourcing",
      "description": "Senior Specialist, Procurement & Sourcing Apply now Job no: 589556 Work type: Full-time Location: Flexible, Geelong - City, Melbourne - Burwood Categories: Information Technology, Finance Enjoy flexible work arrangements with a hybrid model Full-time and continuing $143,627 - $152,229 (HEW 9) + 17% Superannuation Benefits for working with us! At Deakin, we offer more than just a job - we offer a lifestyle. Across our campuses in Geelong, Melbourne, and regional Victoria, you’ll find everything you need to thrive: on-site childcare, gyms, medical centres, cafes, accessible public transport, and convenient parking. Enjoy flexible working arrangements that support your work-life balance, generous leave entitlements including extended parental leave and the option to purchase additional time off, plus a wide range of staff discounts on travel and more. Our health and wellbeing services, ongoing professional development opportunities, and inclusive, supportive culture make Deakin a place where you can grow - whether you're working remotely or immersed in the vibrant energy of campus life. Position overview As the Senior Specialist, Procurement & Sourcing , you will lead strategic sourcing initiatives and develop innovative procurement strategies that deliver cost savings, operational efficiencies, and long-term value across the University. Working closely with stakeholders and suppliers, you will drive supplier performance, manage risk and compliance, champion continuous improvement, and act as a trusted advisor to support informed decision-making and achieve outstanding business outcomes. As a Senior Specialist, Procurement & Sourcing you will: Lead strategic sourcing and procurement activities, including market analysis, supplier evaluation, contract negotiations, and supplier selection to deliver value-driven outcomes. Develop and implement procurement strategies aligned with University objectives, maximising supplier performance, innovation, quality, service levels, and cost effectiveness. Drive commercial and operational results through cost savings, cost avoidance, performance improvements, data analysis, and continuous evaluation of procurement outcomes. Ensure governance, compliance, and risk management, maintaining adherence to policies, legal and ethical requirements while mitigating supplier, contract, and supply chain risks. Build strong stakeholder relationships and lead continuous improvement, acting as a trusted advisor, managing change, coaching others, improving procurement processes and systems, and fostering a high-performance, inclusive culture. To be successful, you’ll have experience in: Strategic sourcing with a strong focus on strategy development, supplier negotiations, and contract management. Property, Construction, Property Technology, Digital & ICT Managing end-to-end procurement processes, from data analysis, identifying needs to supplier selection and contract award. Stakeholder management with the ability to lead, influence and implement sourcing plans that result in cost savings and process efficiencies. Here's how to apply: Only people with the right to work in Australia may apply for this position. Please submit your updated resume and a short cover letter outlining your skills and experience. For a confidential discussion regarding this role, please contact Ash Davies (Senior Manager, Strategic Sourcing) on ash.davies@deakin.edu.au For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD Senior Specialist Procurement Sourcing HEW 9.pdf Applications for this position close on Wednesday 14th October, 11:55pm. Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay at Deakin and contribute to our ongoing success. We value diversity and aim to build an inclusive environment that champions, embraces and respects differences. We support and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and people of all abilities, cultures, sexual orientation, and genders. Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: In accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, appointment to this role is subject to successful completion of relevant pre-employment checks, including Working With Children Checks and candidate gender-based violence declarations. Candidates may be asked to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender‑based Violence, or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender‑based Violence during the course of their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. A declaration is not required from individuals who have experienced gender‑based violence. A ‘Yes’ response does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment, and any information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for relevance to the role and the University’s safety obligations. Advertised: 01 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/949/cw/en/job/589684/senior-project-coordinator-student-complaints-and-conduct": {
      "title": "Senior Project Coordinator, Student Complaints and Conduct",
      "description": "Senior Project Coordinator, Student Complaints and Conduct Apply now Job no: 589684 Work type: Part-time Location: Flexible, Geelong - City, Melbourne - Burwood Categories: Management, Student Services Based at our Melbourne, Burwood Campus / Geelong, Waterfront Campus+ hybrid work arrangements Part-time – 0.80 FTE and fixed-term until Oct 2027 HEW 8 $123,554 - $141,459 + 17% Superannuation Benefits for working with us! At Deakin, we offer more than just a job - we offer a lifestyle. Across our campuses in Geelong, Melbourne, and regional Victoria, you’ll find everything you need to thrive: on-site childcare, gyms, medical centres, cafes, accessible public transport, and convenient parking. Enjoy flexible working arrangements that support your work-life balance, generous leave entitlements including extended parental leave and the option to purchase additional time off, plus a wide range of staff discounts on travel and more. Our health and wellbeing services, ongoing professional development opportunities, and inclusive, supportive culture make Deakin a place where you can grow - whether you're working remotely or immersed in the vibrant energy of campus life. As a Senior Project Coordinator, Student Complaints and Conduct, you will be responsible for responding to and building institutional capacity in the management of current complex, sensitive, and high-risk student matters and to ensure compliance of Student Complaints and Student Conduct functions with recent and incoming (from 1 January 2027) legislative and regulatory requirements. The role is responsible for conducting and facilitating impartial investigations, applying appropriate policies and procedures, effective record-keeping, preparing clear and evidence-based student complaints and grievance outcomes, ensuring compliance with legislative and regulatory requirements and supporting effective risk management. To be successful, you’ll have: Postgraduate qualifications or extensive relevant experience and management expertise; or equivalent combination of experience and/or education/training Demonstrated experience with case management of people with multiple and complex needs. High-level written and oral communication skills, including the ability to produce written information and effective record keeping and evidence management. Demonstrated experience in interpreting and applying policies, procedures, and regulatory frameworks to support consistent, fair, and evidence-based decision-making. High-level interpersonal influence and stakeholder management skills, including demonstrated ability to negotiate and communicate effectively with management, staff, students and other stakeholders Desirable: Graduate or postgraduate qualification or relevant experience in psychology, social work, behavioural science, criminology, law or other related disciplines. Knowledge and experience of the regulatory and governance requirements in higher education. Here's how to apply: Please submit your updated resume and a short cover letter outlining your skills and experience. For a confidential discussion regarding this role, please contact Antonia Lamanna (Director, Student Fairness) on antonia.lamanna@deakin.edu.au For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD-Senior Project Coordinator, Student Complaints & Conduct-589684.pdf Applications for this position close on 14th October 2026 Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay 