    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/949/cw/en/job/589192/join-deakin-law-school-academic-opportunities-across-levels-ad": {
      "title": "Join Deakin Law School | Academic Opportunities Across Levels A-D",
      "description": "Join Deakin Law School | Academic Opportunities Across Levels A-D Apply now Job no: 589192 Work type: Education-focused Academic, Full-time, Level A - Teaching and Research, Level B - Teaching and Research Location: Flexible, Geelong - City, Melbourne - Burwood Categories: Law Based at our Melbourne, Burwood Campus or Waterfront, Geelong Campus Full-time and continuing Level A ($86,599 – $116,417) + 17% superannuation (pro rata, part time) Level B ($122,391 – $144,759) + 17% superannuation (pro rata, part time) Level C ($149,230 – $ 171,602) + 17% superannuation (pro rata, part time) Level D ($179,058 – $ 196,952) + 17% superannuation (pro rata, part time) Deakin Law School Deakin University, located in the cities of Melbourne and Geelong, is committed to educational excellence and innovation that provides transformative learning experiences, and to high quality, high impact research. Deakin Law School, which sits within the Faculty of Business and Law, is a diverse community of scholars teaching and researching in Australian, comparative, transnational and international law. At Deakin you will have access to benefits such as a variety of leave options including generous parental leave and the ability to purchase additional leave; flexible working arrangements to help manage your work-life balance; ongoing learning and development opportunities to grow your career; and an inclusive and supportive culture and environment to work in, both online and on campus. The positions Deakin Law school is looking to appoint several developing or established scholars to ongoing academic positions, both teaching and research and education-focused. Scholars working in all fields of legal teaching and research are welcome to apply, with expertise in the following fields being particularly welcome: Contract Law; Property Law, Equity and Trusts; Torts, Criminal Law; Evidence; Civil Procedure; Foundations of Law; Family Law; and Environmental Law. As an Associate Lecturer (Level A), Lecturer (Level B), Senior Lecturer (Level C), or Associate Professor (Level D) in Deakin Law School you will be actively involved in teaching, including: Delivering student-centred education at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, across a variety of teaching modes (asynchronous, synchronous online, and face-to-face); As a member or a leader of teaching teams, developing and implementing effective and innovative curriculum design and educational resources; Creating and administering a variety of assessment tasks, providing clear assessment criteria and timely feedback to students; Supervising research students (Honours and PhD); Contributing to a culture of collaboration and educational excellence within the Law School, including mentoring of colleagues and building teaching and learning capability. In a teaching and research role, you will also undertake scholarly research, publish in quality journals and secure research funding. By developing a body of work recognised for quality and impact you will build a national reputation. At senior lecturer level or above, you will also participate in and lead collaborations that enable high-quality research with national or international impact and recognition. In an education-focused role, you will contribute to the advancement of knowledge within your field, or in relation to legal pedagogy. You will foster relationships with other academics and universities, the community, government and the legal profession, contributing to the University’s community engagement agenda and enhancing the scholarly reputation of the University. For a comprehensive list of responsibilities for the Level A – D positions and roles, please review the position descriptions in the link below. To be successful, you will have: Key Selection Criteria a PhD in Law (Levels B - D) or substantial progress towards completion of a PhD in Law (Level A); a strong (Level A), or excellent (Levels B, C and D) record of scholarly learning and teaching in undergraduate and/or postgraduate programs, including research supervision; for teaching and research applicants, a developing research agenda (Level A), or an emerging (Level B), national (Level C) or international (Level D) research reputation, underpinned by publications in quality journals and/or success in obtaining research funding; an emerging (Level B), national (Level C) or international (Level D) research reputation, underpinned by publications in quality journals and/or success in obtaining research funding; an ability to contribute to service and leadership within the Law School, commensurate with the role and level sought; an ability to contribute to community engagement around legal research (teaching and research roles) and the teaching of law (all roles); strong interpersonal skills, with an ability to establish good working relationships with colleagues; a commitment to fostering relationships with fellow scholars, the community, the profession, and government, and with other higher educational institutions. How to apply: Please submit your current academic curriculum vitae and a cover letter that clearly states which level and role you are applying for, and detailed responses to the Key Selection Criteria. Position Descriptions for each of the positions available are below: Teaching & Research Level A - Law.pdf Teaching & Research Level B - Law.pdf Teaching & Research Level C - Law.pdf Teaching & Research Level D - Law.pdf Education Focused Level A - Law.pdf Education Focused Level B - Law.pdf Education Focused Level C - Law.pdf Education Focused Level D - Law.pdf For a confidential discussion regarding this role, please contact Professor Patrick Emerton, Dean, Deakin Law School at p.emerton@deakin.edu.au . Applications close on Sunday 8th November at 11.55pm. Advertised: 29 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 08 Nov 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/949/cw/en/job/588670/senior-lecturer-or-associate-professor-centre-for-research-in-assessment-and-digital-learning-cradle": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer or Associate Professor, Centre for Research in Assessment and Digital Learning (CRADLE)",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer or Associate Professor, Centre for Research in Assessment and Digital Learning (CRADLE) Apply now Job no: 588670 Work type: Full-time Location: Melbourne - City Categories: Research Based at Deakin Downtown in Central Melbourne. Easily accessible by tram and train. Full-time and continuing. Generous relocation package and potential visa sponsorship for the right candidate Senior Lecturer - $149,230 - $171,602 (Level C) + 17% superannuation Associate Professor - $179,058 - $196,952 (Level D) + 17% superannuation The Opportunity: We are seeking a passionate Senior Lecturer or Associate Professor to join CRADLE, a globally recognised research centre at the forefront of assessment, feedback and digital innovation in higher education. Drive Deakin’s academic reputation and strategic direction through research leadership, public engagement, policy influence and contribution to the University’s teaching and learning agenda. Lead and shape high-impact research that influence assessment and learning practices across a range of disciplines, enhancing the student experience. About the Centre for Research in Assessment and Digital Learning (CRADLE) CRADLE conducts research in the area of assessment and digital education and collaborates with Deakin Learning Futures and faculties through joint initiatives and with a range of industry partners, other higher education collaborators in Australia and internationally. CRADLE is an Australian and international research leader on assessment in higher education in a digitally connected world. Our team consists of academics with wide-ranging research interests and expertise across assessment and related areas. If you would like to learn more about CRADLE, please visit here . What you will Deliver: Drive teaching and learning excellence by leading innovative research, curriculum development, and assessment practices that enhance student success and educational outcomes. Lead impactful research in assessment, feedback and digital education, securing external funding and translating research into meaningful outcomes. Develop and mentor emerging researchers and academics through doctoral supervision, capability building and creating opportunities for research leadership and career development. Provide strategic leadership and engagement by leading academic teams, fostering cross-disciplinary collaboration, building external partnerships, and contributing to key strategic initiatives. What does this role offer: A Melbourne CBD location that is easily accessible by public transportation. For the right candidate, Deakin can offer visa sponsorship and generous relocation packages both Interstate and Internationally. The opportunity to travel domestically, interstate or overseas to present research or undertake research activities You may be a great fit for this role if you: Key Selection Criteria Completion of a PhD or equivalent qualification; or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training Demonstrated record of achievement (Level C) or significant, impactful and long-standing record of achievement (Level D) in research, teaching and engagement in areas of CRADLE’s priority foci. This includes an internationally and nationally recognised research reputation in assessment and feedback or related areas underpinned by publications in high-quality higher education journals or similar. Experience in securing (Level C) or demonstrated success in securing (Level D) research funding, leading research projects with successful and timely completion Experience in (Level C) or demonstrated track record in (Level D) employing a variety of empirical research methods and innovative conceptual or theoretical framings Experience (Level C) or demonstrated success and passion (Level D) for leadership of teaching, research and/or administration with associated interdisciplinary written and oral communication skills Awareness of drivers of contemporary higher education research and practice, including Indigenous knowledges and generative artificial intelligence Evidence of impact and influence within the discipline and broader academic community Here's how to apply: Please submit your current resume and a short cover letter outlining your skills and experience along with responses to the Key Selection Criteria. Want to Know More? For a confidential discussion, or for further questions regarding this role, please contact Helen Walker, Research Manager via h.walker@deakin.edu.au For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD_Level C_CRADLE.pdf PD_Level D_CRADLE.pdf Applications for this position close at 11.55pm on Monday 26th October. Deakin at a Glance: Deakin is a globally recognised university committed to making a positive impact through education, research and innovation. Our success is driven by our people, and we're dedicated to creating a workplace where individuals feel supported, valued and empowered to do their best work. We offer a collaborative and inclusive culture, opportunities for professional growth, and the flexibility to balance work and life. We welcome applications from people of all backgrounds and are committed to building a diverse workforce that reflects the communities we serve. What we Offer: At Deakin , you'll be supported to thrive both professionally and personally. We offer flexible working arrangements, competitive salary and superannuation benefits, wellbeing initiatives, generous leave provisions, and professional development opportunities to help you achieve your career goals. Join a collaborative and inclusive community that values innovation, flexibility, diversity, and making a positive impact through education, research, and engagement. To find out why our staff love working with Deakin, read more here ! Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: In accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, appointment to this role is subject to successful completion of relevant pre-employment checks, including Working with Children Checks and candidate gender-based violence declarations. As part of Deakin's commitment to providing a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, successful candidates will be required to complete relevant pre-employment checks, which may include a Working with Children Check and declarations relating to gender-based violence in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Any information provided will be treated confidentially and assessed only where relevant to the requirements of the role and Deakin's duty of care obligations. A declaration does not automatically preclude a candidate from employment. Advertised: 28 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 26 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/949/cw/en/job/589518/legal-counsel": {
      "title": "Legal Counsel",
      "description": "Legal Counsel Apply now Job no: 589518 Work type: Full-time Location: Flexible Categories: Legal Services Flexible location at Burwood or Geelong campuses + hybrid work arrangements Full-time and fixed-term for 12 months $143,627 - $152,229 (HEW 9) + 17% Superannuation About the team and role: Our Assurance capability, consisting of Legal Services, Compliance, Contract Governance and Risk develops the University’s assurance frameworks and policies, and provides key expertise that underpins compliance and corporate governance and Deakin's commitment to high standards of integrity. The Legal Services team advises on a range of legal issues across teaching, learning and research, including advisory support and dispute resolution. The Legal Counsel is a member of the University’s Legal Services team, providing expert legal advice and services to stakeholders and associated entities on employment, industrial relations and workplace law matters, including litigious matters. Reporting to the Senior Legal Counsel - Employment, this role will support a key workplace law compliance program, assisting to ensure the University’s compliance with legislation and industrial instruments, protect the University's interests and manage disputes and risk. As a Legal Counsel, you will: Provide expert legal advice on employment, industrial relations and workplace matters, including interpreting and advising on workplace laws, industrial instruments and policies. Draft and review documents, including communications, agreements, templates, tools, and resources. Support investigation and review of workplace practices and assist in the development and implementation of pay rules, remediation methodologies, system and process improvements and compliance controls. Conduct legal research and prepare briefings, reports and guidance for internal stakeholders, supporting informed decision-making and enhancing skills and knowledge across the compliance program. Advise and represent the University in the management and resolution of disputes including through negotiation and/or litigation and managing relationships with external legal providers when required. Support the University in its engagement with external regulators and stakeholders. Identify and mitigate risks and strengthen internal governance and assurance processes, while building strong stakeholder relationships, delivering timely, high-quality legal services with professionalism, confidentiality, and autonomy. To be successful, you’ll have: A Bachelor of Laws degree or other Postgraduate qualifications in law (eg a Juris Doctor) and extensive relevant experience; or equivalent combination of experience and/or education/training Been admitted to practice as an Australian Legal Practitioner within the meaning of the Legal Profession Uniform Law. A current Australian Practising Certificate under the Legal Profession Uniform Law. Strong drafting, communication and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated ability to provide practical solutions to legal problems on a timely basis. Experience and knowledge in relevant area(s) of legal practice Here's how to apply: Only people with the right to work in Australia may apply for this position. Please submit your updated resume and a short cover letter outlining your skills and experience by clicking ‘Apply Now’. For enquiries regarding this role, please contact DeakinLegal@deakin.edu.au For a copy of the position description, please see below: Legal Counsel_PD_HEW 9.pdf Applications for this position close on Sunday, 18 October 2026 at 11:55pm. Benefits for working with us! At Deakin, we offer more than just a job - we offer a lifestyle. Across our campuses in Geelong, Melbourne, and regional Victoria, you’ll find everything you need to thrive: on-site childcare, gyms, medical centres, cafes, accessible public transport, and convenient parking. Enjoy flexible working arrangements that support your work-life balance, generous leave entitlements including extended parental leave and the option to purchase additional time off, plus a wide range of staff discounts on travel and more. Our health and wellbeing services, ongoing professional development opportunities, and inclusive, supportive culture make Deakin a place where you can grow - whether you're working remotely or immersed in the vibrant energy of campus life. Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay at Deakin and contribute to our ongoing success. We value diversity and aim to build an inclusive environment that champions, embraces and respects differences. We support and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and people of all abilities, cultures, sexual orientation, and genders. Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: In accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, appointment to this role is subject to successful completion of relevant pre-employment checks, including Working With Children Checks and candidate gender-based violence declarations. Candidates may be asked to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender‑based Violence, or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender‑based Violence during the course of their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. A declaration is not required from individuals who have experienced gender‑based violence. A ‘Yes’ response does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment, and any information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for relevance to the role and the University’s safety obligations. Advertised: 28 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 18 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/949/cw/en/job/588886/associate-professor-nursing": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Nursing",
      "description": "Associate Professor, Nursing Apply now Job no: 588886 Work type: Full-time Location: Melbourne - Burwood Categories: Health Based at our Melbourne, Burwood Campus + hybrid work arrangements Full-time and continuing Level D $179,058 - $196,952 + 17% Superannuation Benefits for working with us! At Deakin, we offer more than just a job - we offer a lifestyle. Across our campuses in Geelong, Melbourne, and regional Victoria, you’ll find everything you need to thrive: on-site childcare, gyms, medical centres, cafes, accessible public transport, and convenient parking. Enjoy flexible working arrangements that support your work-life balance, generous leave entitlements including extended parental leave and the option to purchase additional time off, plus a wide range of staff discounts on travel and more. Our health and wellbeing services, ongoing professional development opportunities, and inclusive, supportive culture make Deakin a place where you can grow - whether you're working remotely or immersed in the vibrant energy of campus life. Who are we? Deakin is a cutting-edge public university headquartered in Victoria, revolutionising education with 61,000 students across our campuses: Melbourne Burwood, Geelong Waurn Ponds, Geelong Waterfront, Warrnambool, Deakin University Lancaster University Indonesia (DLI), GIFT City, India, and our vibrant online environment. We're proud to be a progressive and open-minded university, delivering the highest student satisfaction in Victoria and consistently ranked in the top 1% of the world's universities. As an Associate Professor, you will: Lead teaching teams to develop innovation in curriculum design to inform unit/courses and materials which influence teaching across discipline within the university. Lead review of units and courses across disciplines within the university and lead refinements. Lead and integrate industry, clinical and/or research practices to inform unit/course design across discipline in peer institutions or nationally. Lead the discovery and adoption of innovative teaching practices at university level and deliver learner-centric, research-informed teaching practices across different levels/modes of delivery. Lead teams and succeed in funding opportunities for research and creative activities, including applications for external competitive funding, external funding for commercialization and translation activities and other funding demonstrating sustained successes. Demonstrate sustained and expanding national and international reputation as amongst world leaders for substantial and growing body of work, recognized quality, excellence and impact with a sustained and expanding track record of timely delivery of outcomes for industry partners. Lead the development and significantly contribute to citizenship activities and effectiveness as champion at local and university level. Represent the university at academic, professional and civic forums. To be successful, you’ll have: Completion of a PhD or equivalent qualification; or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. Registered with the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia as a registered nurse. Distinguished scholarly learning and teaching in UG and PG programs, including innovative curriculum design and supervision to doctoral level. Internationally recognised research reputation underpinned by publications in high-quality journals, and exhibitions where relevant to the discipline. Success in obtaining and timely completion of competitive external research grants. Here's how to apply: Please submit your updated resume, a short cover letter and responses to the Key Selection Criteria. For a confidential discussion regarding this role, please contact Professor Nikki Phillips, Dean of Nursing and Midwifery at nikki.phillips@deakin.edu.au For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD - Associate Professor, Nursing.pdf Applications for this position close on Sunday 18 October 2026. Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay at Deakin and contribute to our ongoing success. We value diversity and aim to build an inclusive environment that champions, embraces and respects differences. We support and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and people of all abilities, cultures, sexual orientation, and genders. Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: In accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, appointment to this role is subject to successful completion of relevant pre-employment checks, including Working With Children Checks and candidate gender-based violence declarations. Candidates may be asked to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender‑based Violence, or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender‑based Violence during the course of their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. A declaration is not required from individuals who have experienced gender‑based violence. A ‘Yes’ response does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment, and any information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for relevance to the role and the University’s safety obligations. Advertised: 18 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Applications close: 18 Oct 2026 AUS Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/949/cw/en/job/589015/senior-teaching-fellow-clinical-educator": {
      "title": "Senior Teaching Fellow (Clinical Educator)",
      "description": "Senior Teaching Fellow (Clinical Educator) Apply now Job no: 589015 Work type: Full-time, Part-time Location: Melbourne - Burwood Categories: Health Based at our Melbourne Burwood Campus + hybrid work arrangements Full-time or part-time and fixed term until 30 June 2027 Level C $149,230 - $171,602 (pro rata part-time) + 17% Superannuation Why this role matters: Join the Deakin University School of Psychology as a Senior Teaching Fellow (Clinical Educator) and play a pivotal role in shaping the future of psychology education and clinical training. This is a unique opportunity to establish and lead a psychology training clinic, creating real-world learning experiences that prepare postgraduate students to become confident, capable and impactful practitioners. In this influential role, you'll combine clinical leadership, teaching excellence and strategic partnership development to strengthen student learning, expand placement opportunities and enhance community engagement. From supervising future psychologists and driving curriculum innovation, to building meaningful collaborations with health and community organisations, you'll help deliver outstanding outcomes for students, the profession and the broader community We're looking for an experienced and passionate clinical educator who thrives on mentoring others, fostering high-quality learning environments and turning new ideas into reality. If you're excited by the opportunity to shape a flagship training initiative, lead innovation in psychology education and leave a lasting legacy for future generations of psychologists, we'd love to hear from you. As a Senior Teaching Fellow (Clinical Educator) you will: Lead the establishment, operation and continuous improvement of a psychology training clinic, ensuring high-quality clinical education and service delivery. Provide clinical supervision and mentoring to postgraduate psychology placement students, supporting their professional development and readiness for practice. Build and strengthen partnerships with health, community and industry organisations to expand placement opportunities and enhance teaching, learning and research outcomes. Drive excellence in teaching and learning through curriculum innovation, quality improvement initiatives and evidence-informed educational practices. Contribute to governance, accreditation and clinical quality processes while fostering a collaborative and inclusive learning environment for students and colleagues. To be successful, you’ll have: General registration as a psychologist with the Psychology Board of Australia, Board-approved supervisor status, and clinical endorsement. Extensive post-registration clinical experience, including psychological assessment and therapy across adult and child/adolescent populations. Demonstrated experience supervising provisional psychologists or placement students in clinical settings. Proven ability to establish, manage or lead clinical services, including governance, quality and risk management. A strong track record in teaching, curriculum development and building partnerships that enhance student and community outcomes. Here's how to apply: Please submit your updated resume, a short cover letter and responses to the Key Selection Criteria. For a confidential discussion regarding this role, please contact Elizabeth Westrupp (Associate Head of School, Research) on elizabeth.westrupp@deakin.edu.au. For a copy of the position description, please see below: PD - Senior Teaching Fellow, 589015.pdf Applications for this position close on Thursday 15th October at 11:55pm. Benefits for working with us! At Deakin, we offer more than just a job. We offer a rewarding career in a flexible, inclusive and forward-thinking environment. Across our campuses in Geelong, Melbourne and regional Victoria, you'll enjoy flexible working arrangements that support work-life balance, generous leave provisions including extended parental leave and the option to purchase additional leave, and access to a range of professional development opportunities to help you grow your career. Are You Ready? Deakin is a Victorian university with a global impact. We are an agile, dynamic, and innovative university committed to making a positive impact through our excellence in education, research and innovation and the contributions we make to the wider community. We understand that our reputation has been built on the dedication and expertise of our staff and we offer a dynamic and diverse working environment with opportunities to grow and develop careers. We believe that a progressive, thriving culture will ensure that people choose to come, and stay at Deakin and contribute to our ongoing success. We value diversity and aim to build an inclusive environment that champions, embraces and respects differences. We support and encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, and people of all abilities, cultures, sexual orientation, and genders. Pre-employment safety and suitability checks: In accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence, appointment to this role is subject to successful completion of relevant pre-employment checks, including Working With Children Checks and candidate gender-based violence declarations. Candidates may be asked to declare whether they have been investigated for an allegation of Gender‑based Violence, or determined to have engaged in conduct that constitutes Gender‑based Violence during the course of their previous employment, or otherwise in a legal process. A declaration is not required from individuals who have experienced gender‑based violence. A ‘Yes’ response does not automatically exclude a candidate from employment, and any information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for relevance to the role and the University’s safety obligations. Advertised: 17 Sep 2026 AUS Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
